[P_06_Hokkaido_CommSummaries]
Speech_0022L=Fisher, if I can't throw the Joint Chiefs a bone, we'll be at war in the next twenty-four. I need you to bring in Zherkezhi for questioning. Milan Nedich has moved him to Hokkaido for protection. I have no idea if Shetland is aware or involved, but I'd like to find out. However it turns out, don't let your personal concerns get in the way.
Speech_0023L=In my opinion, there are too many coincidences here. Zherkezhi is the only living person who could have orchestrated the sinking of the Walsh. Even if the Korea did launch the missile, it would almost certainly have required Zherkezhi's help to actually hit the ship. And this business with Displace... I know you don't want to hear it... but I think Shetland's dirty. The kidnapping of Morgenholt, the protection of Zherkezhi... relocating him after the blackout... it stinks.
Speech_0024L=Looks like Displace has rented out the entire retreat. It's low tech and quiet. Don't expect servers and security. Expect aware guards, in tune with the environment. You're going to need to rely on more traditional methods... up close and personal.
Speech_0025L=Japanese I-SDF conducts low level monitoring of the activities of anyone employed by a PMC for as long as they are in the country. We discovered yesterday that Displace has rented this retreat, and a number of our agents planted microphones in the location. Unfortunately, we were not adequately prepared for the increased importance of the location. The microphones are detectable using standard tools. Needless to say, it would be best if Displace did not find them.
Speech_0026L=North Korean officials continue to deny that the missile attack reported to have struck and destroyer the USS Walsh initiated from within their borders. No counter explanation has yet been offered in face of the overwhelming evidence now coming in from various sources around the world.
Speech_0027L=Reports indicate that over five thousand Americans are still without power in the aftermath of the blackout that struck both Japan and the Eastern United States five nights ago. Electrical workers report ongoing difficulties in sequencing the restart of several large power stations in the Maine, New Hampshire and Rhode Island.
Speech_0001L=LAMBERT - Fisher, if we're going to prevent open war, we need to abduct Zherkezhi and take down Nedich while we're at it.
Speech_0002L=LAMBERT - Fisher, you have civilians up ahead. Watch your fire.
Speech_0003L=LAMBERT - That's two civilians down. This mission is a disaster. Complete your primary objectives and forget about the rest.
Speech_0004L=LAMBERT - You just killed a civilian Fisher. Control yourself.
Speech_0006L=LAMBERT - That's base alert Fisher. Complete your objectives and get to any extraction point.
Speech_0007L=LAMBERT - Fisher, kill Shetland.
Speech_0008L=LAMBERT - Fisher...objective update...take down Shetland.
Speech_0009L=LAMBERT - Shetland escaped. Complete the mission.
Speech_0010L=LAMBERT - There was no way you could have stopped Shetland. We'll try and track him...complete the mission and get out of there.
Speech_0011L=LAMBERT - That's Nedich out of the picture and there is nothing we could have done to prevent Shetland escaping. Get to extraction.
Speech_0012L=LAMBERT - Nedich is taken care of, but Shetland is on his way there. I don't know why, but I want to find out what he and Zherkezhi are meeting about.
Speech_0013L=LAMBERT - Satellite show you nearing Zherkezhi.
Speech_0014L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Good job Sam. That's the last of the microphones that Otomo asked us to recover.
Speech_0015L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Zherkezhi is dead Sam...there's nothing we could have done to save him.
Speech_0016L=REDDING - Scanning the license plates ID's Nedich for us. Carry on.
Speech_0017L=REDDING - Sam, use your EEV to scan the license plates on those trucks so I can dig up some info on our friend Nedich.
Speech_0018L=REDDING - Fisher...just ID'd Nedich, AKA Milos Nowak... suspected war criminal from the Bosnian conflict. Your orders stand.
Speech_0019L=REDDING - That's all your primary objectives Fisher, we can extract you any time.
Speech_0020L=REDDING - Sam, we can't extract you until you've completed your primary objectives.
Speech_0021L=LAMBERT - Fisher...we just got word from Admiral Otomo at Japanese I-SDF. Some of his agents left behind microphones at the retreat and they're worried about Displace finding them. See if you can recover them.

